{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-zerospeed-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.62: `project-zerospeed`, a PROJECT-domain run with an on-network link of ZERO average speed -- link 2, an idling queue at a stop line -- beside its 25 mph approach, link 1, both on road type 5, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its PROJECT input database (`inputs/washtenaw-project-zerospeed.esm`). It selects source types 21 (gasoline) and 62 (diesel), road type 5, running THC, CO, NOx and Total Energy, brake wear and tire wear (PM10 and PM2.5).\n\nWHAT IT EXERCISES: for a link whose linkAvgSpeed is not positive LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator writes itself a drive schedule of thirty seconds at speed 0 and grade 0 (java:343-367) and walks it (java:378): every second is mode 501, which is mode 1 at fraction 1 for every running polProcess and stays under the temp source types for brake wear, so the queue has NO brake-wear row (`lsl_isIdleSchedule`, `lsl_brakeGap`). ProjectTAG's SHO takes its `else` arm: the link-volume product with no travel-time share (`link_travel_hours_share`). Tire wear's project generator gives the queue mode 400 (`lomd_tireW`). Before the port the model refused it (`run_projectZeroSpeedLinks` 1).\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 2444. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain"
    ]
  },
